🟡 **Severity: MEDIUM**

`FeeSetup::toFees()` in `Config.h` only passes `{referenceFee, accountReserve, ownerReserve}` to the `Fees` constructor, leaving `gasLimit`, `bytecodeSizeLimit`, and `gasPrice` at their struct default of **0**. All callers (including production genesis in `Application.cpp`) therefore write zeros to the FeeSettings ledger entry, silently ignoring the operator's configured gas-fee values.
Helpful? Add 👍 / 👎

<details>
<summary>💡 Fix Suggestion</summary>

**Suggestion:** Update `FeeSetup::toFees()` in `src/xrpld/core/Config.h` (around line 94) to propagate the gas-related fields. Currently it returns `Fees{referenceFee, accountReserve, ownerReserve}` which uses the 3-argument constructor, leaving `gasLimit`, `bytecodeSizeLimit`, and `gasPrice` at their struct defaults of 0.

Either:
1. Add a 6-argument constructor to `Fees` in `include/xrpl/protocol/Fees.h` that also accepts `gasLimit`, `bytecodeSizeLimit`, and `gasPrice`, and use it in `toFees()`.
2. Or, update `toFees()` to construct the `Fees` object and then set the gas fields individually, e.g.:
```cpp
[[nodiscard]] Fees
toFees() const
{
    Fees f{referenceFee, accountReserve, ownerReserve};
    f.gasLimit = gasLimit;
    f.bytecodeSizeLimit = bytecodeSizeLimit;
    f.gasPrice = gasPrice;
    return f;
}
```

This ensures that operator-configured gas values (defaults: gasLimit=1'000'000, bytecodeSizeLimit=100'000, gasPrice=1'000'000) are correctly propagated to genesis ledger construction and any other callers of `toFees()`.

</details>
